## Axis D — #84 tiles name the building

Fix: `src/ui/graph-flow.ts` — `StageNodeData` gains `machineName: string | null`
(:64-70); a `machineNameOf` helper beside `recipeNameOf` (:284-...) returns null
under the SAME conditions as recipeNameOf (no recipeId / dangling id) else
`catalog.machines[recipe.machineId]?.displayName ?? recipe.machineId` (the raw-id
fallback), wired into the node `data` (:645). `src/ui/GraphCanvas.tsx` — the
machines span renders `×{machineCount} {machineName}` (:154-160, gated on
recipeName as before).
Tests:
  data (`src/ui/graph-flow.test.ts`):
    - "machineName resolves the machine displayName (#84)"
    - "machineName falls back to the raw machineId when off the machine table (#84)"
    - "machineName is null for a recipe-less stage … (#84)"
  render (`src/ui/smoke.test.tsx` › GraphCanvas SSR):
    - "names the building on the tile: ×N MachineName (#84)" — RF12 SSR through
      the real GraphCanvas (getInitialState seam stubbed with a 20-Smelter
      Iron-Ingot stage) asserts `<span class="stage-node-machines">×20
      Smelter</span>`.

- PASS: fix in → graph-flow 48 passed; the #84 SSR pin passes.
- BREAK 1 (GraphCanvas drops the name → bare `×{machineCount}`): the SSR pin
  FAILED:
  > `expected '…' to contain '<span class="stage-node-machines">×20 Smelter</span>'`
  > (rendered `<span class="stage-node-machines">×20</span>` — recipe line still
  > "Iron Ingot", so the recipe resolved; only the name was dropped).
- BREAK 2 (machineNameOf returns null instead of the raw-id fallback): the
  off-table fallback data pin FAILED:
  > `AssertionError: expected null to be 'smelter'`
  > (the resolved recipe's off-table machineId no longer falls back — the exact
  > dangling-"×N " risk the fallback idiom prevents).
- RESTORE (both) → graph-flow 48 + the #84 SSR pin green.
